            <ArticleTitle>Plasma tryptophan and musculoskeletal pain in non-articular rheumatism (&quot;fibrositis syndrome&quot;).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>65-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Plasma-free tryptophan is inversely related to the severity of subjective pain in 8 patients who fulfilled criteria for a variety of non-articular rheumatism, the &quot;fibrositis syndrome&quot;. The observation is consistent with animal and human studies suggesting a relationship between reduced brain serotonin metabolism and pain reactivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
